<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palaiologos dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Palaiologan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palaiologos dynasty was the last ruling dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, from 1261 until the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1453. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII</a> recovered Constantinople from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latins</a> in 1261. Accounts of the Byzantine Empire describe the Palaiologan state as more a city-state than an empire, dependent on Genoese commercial privileges.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palaiologos-dynasty.jpg" alt="Palaiologos dynasty" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Byzantine_Palaiologos_Eagle.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
